            "width": 702,
            "height": 961,
            "visibility": "show_all",
            "draggable": true,
            "presentation_state": "show_all",
            "properties": {
                "0": {
                    "name": "block",
                    "value": "cmy_to_rgb converts a colour described as cyan, magenta, yellow\ninto the same colour described as red, green, blue.\n\nAn orange of [0, 0.5, 1] in cmy comes out as [1, 0.5, 0] in rgb.\nIn the demo, one component of the cmy colour sweeps steadily while the other two\nhold still; the vectors show the colour going in and coming out, and the swatch\nshows the colour itself.\n\nUse it to show or send a cmy colour as light. It is the simplest conversion\nthere is: each value is one minus the cmy one.\n\nTHE TWO SPACES:\n\ncmy   cyan, magenta, yellow - the inverse of rgb, how inks subtract light.\n      Each value is simply one minus the rgb one.\nrgb   red, green, blue - how a screen makes light.\n      Natural for output, awkward for adjustment: there is no component\n      that means \"brightness\" or \"how vivid\".\n\nSYNTAX:\ncmy_to_rgb\n\nEXAMPLE:\ncmy_to_rgb\n\nINPUTS and PARAMETERS:\n\nin:\nThree numbers - a list, or a NumPy array - in the cmy space. Receiving data\nhere triggers the conversion.\n\nfrom / to:\nThe spaces being converted between: rgb, cmy, hsl or hsv. The node's name sets\nthem to cmy and rgb; the menus can repoint it to any other pair\nwithout replacing the node.\n\nin scale / out scale:\nWhat numeric range the values use, INDEPENDENTLY at each end:\n\n  0-1     0.0 to 1.0, the usual choice inside a patch\n  0-100   percentages, as design tools tend to use\n  0-255   bytes, as image files and many devices use\n\nBecause the two are separate, the node also does the rescaling for you:\nset in scale to 0-255 and out scale to 0-1 to bring an image's colours into\npatch range in the same move as the conversion.\n\nOUTPUTS:\n\nout:\nThe converted colour: three numbers (a NumPy array) in the rgb space and the out scale.\n\nOUT OF RANGE:\nValues are converted through rgb, and red, green and blue are held to 0 to 1\non the way, so a component pushed past its range gives the nearest colour\nthat exists rather than an error.\n\nSEE ALSO:\nrgb_to_cmy    the reverse conversion\ncmy_to_hsl    cmy to hue, saturation, lightness\ncmy_to_hsv    cmy to hue, saturation, value\ncolor_convert    choose both spaces yourself\ncolor            pick a colour, or show one",
                    "value_type": "string"
                },
                "1": {
                    "name": "lock",
                    "value": true,
                    "value_type": "bool"
                },
                "2": {
                    "name": "width",
                    "value": 694,
                    "value_type": "int"
                },
                "3": {
                    "name": "height",
                    "value": 945,
                    "value_type": "int"
                },
                "4": {
